; ds4-paris-probe.fk — the cheapest test that can refute a whole forward pass,
; and the confound that means it has not yet.
;
; ══ CORRECTION, 2026-07-28, same day, after Urs: "we can find on the internet
; ══ how to prompt those models, we don't have to guess."
;
; This cell first concluded THE FORWARD IS DEFECTIVE. That conclusion is
; WITHDRAWN, and the reason is a defect in OUR code, not the model's.
;
; DeepSeek-V4-Flash's own MODEL_CARD (~/models/ds4-engine/MODEL_CARD.md, lines
; 145-180) gives the format, and it is not raw text:
;     <｜begin▁of▁sentence｜><｜User｜>...<｜Assistant｜></think>
; where the immediate </think> selects non-thinking mode.
;
; Encoding exactly that string through this body's own tokenizer returns 34 ids
; where it should return roughly 15, because tkz-encode BPEs the special markers
; as ORDINARY TEXT:
;     30="<"  28217="｜"  8277="begin"  5487/226="▁" fragments  2154="of"
; `<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>` is one token in this vocabulary and our encoder never
; emits it. There is no special-token table in dsv4-tokenizer.fk's encode path.
;
; SO: this model has never once been given a correctly-formed prompt by this
; body. The degenerate output below is real and unexplained — it may be the
; forward, or it may be a model asked in a shape it has never seen. Those are
; different findings and the probe as run cannot tell them apart.
;
; THE GAP THIS OPENS, named where it will be found: dsv4-tokenizer.fk needs a
; special-token pass BEFORE BPE — match the vocabulary's atomic markers first,
; BPE only the text between them. Until that exists, no prompt-shaped claim
; about this model is admissible.
;
; ══ AND THEN THE CONFOUND WAS REMOVED, same day, and the finding CAME BACK.
;
; The special ids were found by scanning the vocabulary itself rather than by
; encoding: id 0 renders `<eginfentence`, which is `<｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>` with
; characters dropped by our own renderer. So:
;     0       <｜begin▁of▁sentence｜>      1    <｜end▁of▁sentence｜>
;     128803  <｜User｜>                   128804  <｜Assistant｜>
;     128821  <think>                     128822  </think>
; and a correct non-thinking prompt was assembled BY ID, bypassing the broken
; encoder entirely:
;     0 · 128803 · <ascii text ids> · 128804 · 128822
;
; Run 2026-07-28, 26 steps, 171 s, VERDICT PASS 124 gates. The answer to
; "What is the capital of France? Answer with one word.":
;     " Protocol syn Political with the Protocol Politics के オリ Participate in"
;
; The prompt is correct. The ASCII text ids decode back exactly. The output is
; still incoherent. THE FORWARD PASS IS DEFECTIVE, and this time the most
; plausible alternative has been eliminated rather than assumed away.
;
; ONE RESIDUAL, named rather than hidden: our renderer demonstrably mishandles
; 3-byte UTF-8, and encode and decode share that mapping. A round trip cannot
; validate a codec whose two halves hold the same wrong assumption — the errors
; compensate and the test passes. It happens that this prompt is pure ASCII,
; where the path is sound, so the residual does not reach this result. It would
; reach any non-ASCII prompt.
;
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS. The DS4 stones stood on `selfgauge`: no tool on this machine
; reads GGUF types 40/41, so a whole-forward output has no reference to be
; checked against, and 110 gates therefore certify internal consistency and
; nothing else. I repeated that as "correctness is unknowable here". Urs:
; "unknowable here?"
;
; It was a manufactured blocker, and it had two exits I had not tried.
;
; EXIT ONE, TESTED AND CLOSED. `~/models/ds4-engine/ds4` is BUILT — 1 852 672
; bytes, dated 2026-07-24 — and receipts/2026-07-21-ds4-metal-gap-map.md says in
; its own radius note "I did not run ds4 once." So the claim that ds4 refuses
; this file was inherited, never witnessed. Run 2026-07-28 it warns on every
; type-40 expert tensor and then stops hard:
;     ds4: tensor output.weight has type unknown, expected q8_0, q4_K, or q4_0
; The blocker is real. It is now a measurement rather than a rumour.
;
; EXIT TWO, OPEN THE WHOLE TIME. An implementation oracle is not the only kind.
; "The capital of France is" is completed by " Paris" by every competent language
; model, and knowing that requires no reference implementation — it is knowledge
; of the WORLD, not of a program. A forward pass that fails it is wrong, and no
; chat template, special token or prompt form can rescue it, because this is a
; plain continuation with nothing to template.
;
; THE PROBE, run 2026-07-28 through metal_dsv4_stack.sh with prompt prefill:
;   prompt      671 "The" · 6102 " capital" · 294 " of" · 8760 " France" · 344 " is"
;   generated   270 " the" · 128981 "<|place_holder_mm_span_0155|>" · 3675 "pped" · 418 " with"
;
; The tokenization round-trips exactly to the input text, so the encoder is not
; the fault. The third emission is a PLACEHOLDER SPECIAL TOKEN — mass landing
; where no trained model puts it for this context. The 43-layer forward is
; defective, and the defect is invisible to every one of the 110 gates because
; each asks whether the machine did what the recipe says and none asks whether
; the recipe is the model's.
;
; WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO. It does not localize. It says the pipeline is wrong, not
; which of 43 layers, which regime, or which decode. It is a smoke alarm, not a
; diagnosis — and a smoke alarm that costs 118 s is worth running before any
; further stone is placed on this lane.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk

(do
    ; the prompt, as the body's own tokenizer encodes it
    (defn dpp-prompt-ids () (list 671 6102 294 8760 344))
    (defn dpp-prompt-text () "The capital of France is")
    ; what the run emitted, 2026-07-28
    (defn dpp-observed () (list 270 128981 3675 418))
    ; the id of the token any competent model would rank first here is not known
    ; to this cell — and it does not need to be. The claim is weaker and enough:
    ; a SPECIAL/placeholder token in the first four emissions of a plain factual
    ; continuation is not something a trained model does.
    (defn dpp-placeholder-id () 128981)
    (defn dpp-emitted-placeholder? ()
        (dpp-memq (dpp-placeholder-id) (dpp-observed)))
    (defn dpp-memq (x xs) (if (eq (len xs) 0) 0 (if (eq (head xs) x) 1 (dpp-memq x (tail xs)))))

    ; the verdict this probe carries
    ; WITHDRAWN: this said `forward-suspect?`. The observation stands; the inference
    ; does not, because the prompt was malformed upstream of it.
    (defn dpp-observation-stands? () (dpp-emitted-placeholder?))
    ; what the probe can honestly claim today
    (defn dpp-forward-defect-established? () 1)   ; re-established with the prompt confound removed
    (defn dpp-confounded-by-prompt-form? () 0)   ; the correct prompt was run; output unchanged
    (defn dpp-tokenizer-handles-specials? () 0)
    ; and the two exits, recorded so neither is inherited again
    (defn dpp-ds4-engine-built? () 1)          ; witnessed 2026-07-28
    (defn dpp-ds4-engine-runs-file? () 0)      ; witnessed: refuses output.weight
    (defn dpp-behavioural-oracle-available? () 1)
    ; the correctly-formed prompt, by id, and what it produced
    (defn dpp-bos () 0)
    (defn dpp-user-mark () 128803)
    (defn dpp-assistant-mark () 128804)
    (defn dpp-nothink-mark () 128822)
    (defn dpp-correct-prompt-run? () 1)
    (defn dpp-correct-prompt-observed ()
        (list 29326 8317 21774 418 270 29326 28328 34887 121141 114070 295))
    ; the renderer's 3-byte UTF-8 defect, which the round trip cannot see
    (defn dpp-renderer-utf8-3byte-ok? () 0)
    (defn dpp-roundtrip-can-validate-codec? () 0)
    0)
